{"seq":1263,"lane":"B","class":"unhelpful-evidence","severity":"serious","evidence":"traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1263.json, e3: “The next day she toured the Beijing robot exhibition, drawing onlookers the way her father does on his Asia trips, watching robots do flying kicks and stopping by the booths of Chinese companies built on Nvidia technology.” Filed under v2, NVIDIA FY2027 total revenue.","rule":"docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html §5.1 and §5.3: keep statements an analyst would note for a question; background without a connection to its answer is not evidence.","mechanism":"B treated a visit to an exhibition as a revenue driver without showing how the visit changes NVIDIA's revenue."}
{"seq":1263,"lane":"B","class":"weak-period-link","severity":"minor","evidence":"traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1263.json, e2: “But Jensen Huang expects it to grow ten-fold within a decade.” Filed under v72, NVIDIA FY2028 total revenue.","rule":"docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html §5.1 and D259: evidence must have a logical connection to the answer; distant forecasts may be retained but their weight is judged separately.","mechanism":"B linked a decade-long physical-AI forecast to next year's company-wide revenue without a trajectory for that year. It is at most a weak indication of longer-term opportunity."}
{"seq":1265,"lane":"B","class":"invented-statement-date","severity":"serious","evidence":"traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1265.json: “Colette Kress, Nvidia's chief financial officer, told analysts the company expects revenue growth of 70% in its 2028 financial year” and “Huang said demand was much greater than 70%”; both records set original_day to “2026-08-27”.","rule":"docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html §2 and D220: preserve the original statement day; leave it unknown when the article does not state it.","mechanism":"B appears to have used the August 27 share-price move as the day of both remarks, although the article does not say they were made that day."}
{"seq":1266,"lane":"A","class":"missed-annual-revenue-question","severity":"serious","evidence":"traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1266.json: “The company guided to $3.15 billion for Q3 revenue, and increased their fiscal 2027 and fiscal 2028 revenue expectations to approximately $12 billion and $18 billion.” A returned “questions”: [].","rule":"docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html §3 A and §4: an important company-wide annual business quantity can merit its own question when its outcome can move independently of existing questions; company quantities use this or next fiscal year.","mechanism":"A did not propose tracking Marvell's annual revenue despite the article's two explicit annual expectations. The open NVIDIA accelerator-share question v82 does not settle Marvell's revenue."}
{"seq":1266,"lane":"B","class":"broader-question-also-linked","severity":"serious","evidence":"traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1266.json, e5: “Broadcom's fiscal Q2 AI semiconductor revenue grew 143% year-over-year to reach $10.8 billion … Broadcom projects $16 billion for its Q3 AI semiconductor revenue”. The writer linked it to both v2, NVIDIA total revenue, and v82, NVIDIA's accelerator-market share.","rule":"docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html §5.1 and the filing rule in D207: use the narrowest connected question; do not also file the same competition evidence under a broader company-wide revenue question.","mechanism":"B returned both links, and the handover retained them because the existing narrowing check did not recognise these two questions as a broader and narrower pair."}
{"seq":1266,"lane":"matching","class":"different-facts-marked-repeat","severity":"serious","evidence":"traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1266.json, e5: “Broadcom projects $16 billion for its Q3 AI semiconductor revenue”; Jev marked the whole passage repeat of e808, whose stored quote says “AVGO printed $10.8 billion in AI semiconductor revenue last quarter, up 143%”.","rule":"docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html §2 and D202/D204: distinguish the same statement from an additional or revised statement; retain each source record and its relationship faithfully.","mechanism":"Jev matched the shared Q2 figure and labelled the entire passage a repeat even though it also contains a separate Q3 forecast. The writer stores both records, but their repeat relationship misdescribes the new information."}
{"seq":1266,"lane":"matching","class":"different-facts-marked-repeat","severity":"serious","evidence":"traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1266.json, e6: “Revenue for Q2 grew by 50 percent to $11.54 billion, with Data Center revenue more than doubling to $6.72 billion. Management projects Q3 revenue at $13 billion”; Jev marked it repeat of e3072: “AMD’s data centre revenue more than doubled last quarter to $6.7bn.”","rule":"docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html §2 and D202/D204: a repeat relationship must describe the same statement, not erase distinctions between additional figures and guidance.","mechanism":"Jev matched the overlapping Data Center figure and treated a passage containing total revenue and separate Q3 guidance as the same statement. The writer retains both records, but the relationship is misleading."}
{"seq":1267,"lane":"B","class":"missed-deal-development","severity":"serious","evidence":"traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1267.json: “In early negotiations, Nvidia had planned to spend billions of dollars to purchase licenses for some of Perplexity's technology and absorb some of its employees. But the talks ultimately pivoted toward a more conventional equity investment path.” B did not return this passage for v62, the pending Perplexity equity investment.","rule":"docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html §5.1: retain a named party's reported action or change in a pending arrangement when it helps assess an open question; preserve uncertainty.","mechanism":"B captured the financing-round valuation but missed the reported change in the negotiations' structure, which helps explain the proposed equity transaction."}
{"seq":1268,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"non-standalone-summary","severity":"minor","evidence":"traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1268.json, e1: the source gives “operating income … $8.8 billion” and margin “35.6% from 20.7%”; the stored one_line says only “The Q2 operating income and margin expansion support the possibility of a higher FY2026 margin, though the quarter does not establish the full-year result.”","rule":"docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html §2: evidence needs a standalone summary of the statement, alongside the quote and provenance.","mechanism":"A's what_it_shows interpretation was copied into the stored summary without the reported figures. The exact figures remain in the quote and are available to the judge."}
{"summary":{"items_read":[1261,1262,1263,1264,1265,1266,1267,1268],"classes":{"unhelpful-evidence":1,"weak-period-link":1,"invented-statement-date":1,"missed-annual-revenue-question":1,"broader-question-also-linked":1,"different-facts-marked-repeat":2,"missed-deal-development":1,"non-standalone-summary":1}}}